    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the single test class, 2 tests, plus a clean build). \n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `locality` derivation from an owner's city using the fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD, else `UNKNOWN`).\n\nChanges, chosen to keep structural impact low:\n\n1. **New `Locality` helper** (`rest/function/owner/Locality.java`) \u2014 a small, cohesive static class (WMC_other = 0) holding the city\u2192region map, mirroring the existing `Address` helper. All the new complexity lives here in an isolated unit rather than growing an existing method.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `Locality.of(owner)`, exactly matching the established pattern for the other pure single-field derivations (`householdId`, `membershipNumber`). This routes locality into *every* owner response (get/list/created/updated) with no changes to any responder function.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO gets the `setLocality` setter the mapper needs.\n\nI put the derivation in the mapper rather than in `RespondWithOwner` because locality depends only on the entity's city (like `householdId`/`membershipNumber`, which are also mapper expressions) and needs no repository lookup \u2014 this both keeps the changed method's surrounding complexity minimal and makes the field consistent across all owner representations. Both acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity`, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown`) pass and the build is green.",
